# Titan Orbit — Toroidal map

The playable map is a **torus on XZ**. Dynamic movers **wrap** into the canonical rectangle
`[-MapWidth/2, MapWidth/2) × [-MapHeight/2, MapHeight/2)`. There is **one entity** and **one collider**
per body — no tiled visual or collider copies. Deep dive: `Docs/TITAN-ORBIT-COMPLETE-COURSE.md` §11.4.

---

## Two layers (do not mix)

| Layer | Behavior | API |
|-------|----------|-----|
| **Sim / hulls** | After Unity.Physics integrates, wrap ships, bullets, gems, rockets, transports. Display follows that wrapped pose. | `ToroidalMapEcs.Wrap` |
| **Ranges / aim** | Orbit, dock, combat, beams, transports, minimap still use **shortest path on the torus** (a planet on +X still owns a ship that wrapped to −X). | `ShortestOffsetXZ`, `ToroidalDistance`, `ToroidalDirection` |

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — Euclidean range across opposite edges (misses / false “far”)
float d = math.distance(ship.xz, planet.xz);

// ✅ GOOD — toroidal shortest path for gameplay reach
float d = ToroidalMapEcs.ToroidalDistance(ship, planet, mapW, mapH);

// ✅ GOOD — wrap movers into the rectangle (sim = visual = collider)
transform.Position = ToroidalMapEcs.Wrap(transform.Position, mapW, mapH);

// ❌ BAD — nearest-tile display copies / hysteresis retile
displayPos = ToroidalMapEcs.GetDisplayPosition(logicalPos, localShipPos, mapW, mapH);
```

Hull contacts are **Unity.Physics** (compound ship hulls, baked world spheres). Do not add
`ShipToroidalWorldCollision*` sphere-resolve unless playtest re-opens a documented seam fallback.
A wrap that lands inside a solid uses a one-tick depenetrate against the **real** `PhysicsCollider`.

Camera / presentation treat a ±map-size jump as a **snap** (same-frame camera delta + short fade/warp).
Do not lerp remotes or local display coast the long way across the map.

